Overall Assessment: Recommend

I recommend the candidate for the Product Owner role.

The candidate demonstrated a good understanding of the key technical aspects of the role, particularly around Transaction Monitoring, ML integration and the importance of balancing detection effectiveness with operational efficiency.

Having been involved in the development of an ML model, they have gained valuable practical experience and demonstrated a good understanding of the development lifecycle, technical dependencies, performance monitoring and the requirements for successful deployment. They also showed an appreciation of the need to balance business requirements, technical constraints and governance considerations when prioritising solutions.

My main area of concern is around confidence and the ability to challenge stakeholders when required. The candidate came across as relatively reserved during the interview, and I was not fully convinced they would consistently feel comfortable challenging decisions or pushing back on competing requirements. This is particularly important for a Product Owner operating across multiple teams and stakeholders, where clear communication, influencing and the ability to drive decisions are essential.

That said, I believe this is an area that could be developed with experience, coaching and greater exposure to senior stakeholders, rather than a fundamental limitation.

Overall, the candidate demonstrated sufficient technical understanding and relevant experience to succeed in the role. While I see an opportunity to further develop their confidence and stakeholder influencing skills, I am comfortable recommending them.

Recommendation: Recommend.







Overall Assessment: Recommend

I recommend the candidate for the Product Owner role.

The candidate demonstrated a strong understanding of the key technical aspects of the role and was able to address most of the questions confidently. In particular, they showed a good appreciation of the trade-offs between rules-based and ML-driven detection approaches, the importance of data quality, observability and performance monitoring, and the need to balance technical capabilities with business requirements.

What stood out was their structured, data-driven approach and strong strategic thinking. They demonstrated an ability to step back, consider the bigger picture and assess different options rather than focusing solely on the immediate technical solution. They also came across as confident and comfortable discussing complex topics, which I believe will be valuable when working across multiple teams and challenging stakeholders.

One potential development area is their limited direct experience owning a product involving ML and AI capabilities. While they demonstrated sufficient technical understanding, they may initially need some support navigating the specific challenges of managing the end-to-end product lifecycle, including prioritisation, governance and delivery of ML-driven solutions.

Overall, I was impressed by their analytical approach, confidence and strategic vision. I believe they have the right foundations to succeed in the role, and their limited direct exposure to ML/AI product ownership is something they should be able to develop.

Recommendation: Recommend.
